From: Camera investigation <camera-investigation@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH candidate] arm64: dts: qcom: denali: describe rear camera rotation

The rear OV13858 image on the revision-24 safe ISO was reported upside
down with no sensor-rotation control. Describe the 180-degree correction
as a candidate derived from that report. Verify it with an asymmetric
physical target before promotion.

The existing orientation property specifies the camera location, not the
rotation. The v4l2 fwnode control path exposes this property as
V4L2_CID_CAMERA_SENSOR_ROTATION. The v0.7.2 simple pipeline cannot rotate
pixels on this sensor without writable flip controls; userspace must
honour the reported orientation or supply a separate conversion step.
This patch does not change either sensor stream or its privacy LED.

Evidence: hardware/cameras/evidence/2026-11-03-rev24-quality-orientation.md
Reference: the video-interface-devices.yaml media DT binding
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi
@@ -945,6 +945,7 @@
 		avdd-supply = <&vreg_l5m_2p8>;
 
 		orientation = <1>;
+		rotation = <180>;
 
